{# IN·20 — the month, with one mark per incident.

   FILLED IS OPEN AND HOLLOW IS CLOSED — the same reading the map plate uses, so
   a mark means one thing across the product. Clicking a mark opens the case
   file; "+N more" and the day itself lead to the register showing this window.

   THE MONTH COMES FROM THE SHARED FILTER ROW and this card has no control of
   its own: the stepper's arrows are drawn and not offered, because stepping
   here would move the map, the register and every chart beside it without
   saying so. Changing the month is the filter row's job
   ({@see IncidentFilter::toQuery}, `month=YYYY-MM`).

   THE GRID IS THE ATLAS'S. The day head, the cell, its fixed height, the day
   number and the "+N more" are `atlas_calendar()`'s — which is the whole reason
   a busy week cannot make this month taller than a quiet one. This module hands
   over everything it has for a day ({@see IncidentCalendar}) and is never asked
   how many marks fit. #}
<div class="c" data-w="cal">
    {{ atlas_calendar(
        dashboard.calendar,
        title: 'Incidents calendar',
        today: now,
        caption: 'Filled is open, hollow is closed. Clicking a mark opens the case file; the month is whatever the filter row is showing.'
    ) }}
</div>
